.* SYSTEM: the task menu for the general system tasks.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='SYSTEM'.
:IMPORT NAME=DSPMSG PNLGRP=QHMHCMD.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=SYSTEM HELP=HLPSYSTEM KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.General System Tasks
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='MENU JOB' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT1'.Jobs
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU STATUS' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT2'.Status
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD DSPMSG MSGQ(*SYSOPR)' HELP=DSPMSG.Display system operator messages
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU MESSAGE' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT4'.Messages
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU DATA' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT5'.Files, libraries, and folders
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='MENU SAVE' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT6'.Save
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='MENU RESTORE' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT7'.Restore
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='MENU DEVICE' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT8'.Device operations
:MENUI OPTION=9 ACTION='MENU CMN' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT9'.Communications
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='MENU SECURITY' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT10'.Security
:MENUI OPTION=60 ACTION='MENU SYSTEM2' HELP='SYSTEM/OPT60'.More system task options
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPSYSTEM.General System Tasks - Help
:P.The everyday operation of the system: jobs, status, messages, saving and
restoring, devices and security. Option 60 shows more.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows menu MAIN.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT1'.Jobs
:P.Option 1. Shows menu JOB&colon. Jobs.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT2'.Status
:P.Option 2. Shows menu STATUS&colon. Status.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT4'.Messages
:P.Option 4. Shows menu MESSAGE&colon. Messages.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT5'.Files, libraries, and folders
:P.Option 5. Shows menu DATA&colon. Files, libraries, and folders.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT6'.Save
:P.Option 6. Shows menu SAVE&colon. Save.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT7'.Restore
:P.Option 7. Shows menu RESTORE&colon. Restore.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT8'.Device operations
:P.Option 8. Shows menu DEVICE&colon. Device operations.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT9'.Communications
:P.Option 9. Shows menu CMN&colon. Communications.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT10'.Security
:P.Option 10. Shows menu SECURITY&colon. Security.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SYSTEM/OPT60'.More system task options
:P.Option 60. Shows menu SYSTEM2&colon. More system task options.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
